issues.body:
Follow-up to #9798.

Today a task-curation declaration pins its agent environment with an `AgentImage("ghcr.io/...@sha256:...")` literal, while the grader image is an `ImageRecipe` under `experiments/post_training/task_curation/images/` that the prelaunch build command builds, pushes to the public `iris-task` package and records as an artifact. Agent images should work the same way:

- one `ImageRecipe` per family (TaskTrove executable code, nl2bash, the Python test images) next to its Dockerfile, built by `python -m experiments.post_training.task_curation.images --recipe <name>`;
- declarations reference the recipe, and the converter reads the built digest from the conversion context the way it reads `grader_environment`, so the TaskSpec environment carries a pullable, digest-pinned reference;
- the artifact identity already hashes the built digest, so a recipe change rebuilds the family.

Also needed for the SWE-style sources (swe_rebench, swesmith, the Nemotron Ultra SWE pivots), which carry no image and no grader today and never reach `final/`: a per-row image reference from the archive plus a grader, which is a separate piece of work but depends on the recipe mechanism.
